Upstream bug: a native Responses stream cancelled before any output text or
tool arguments reached the client never reaches spend logging. Partial billing
(https://github.com/BerriAI/litellm/pull/47611) only covers streams that
delivered output, so a cancellation during reasoning leaves no row.

Record that cancellation as a 499 failure through native failure callbacks and
the proxy failure hook, which persists the row and releases the request slot;
final usage stays unknown. Cancellations after output stay with upstream's
partial billing.

Removal check: tests/verify_responses_disconnect.py

